The utility is used to control Netwave AirSurfer PC Cards as well
as  display statistics.  The following options are available: Set
the domain of the card to The domain must be  between  0x000  and
0x1ff.  The domains 0x000 through 0x0ff are for access to an add‐
hoc network.  The domains 0x100 through 0x1ff are for access to a
Netwave  Access  Point.  The default domain is 0x000.  A card may
only talk to the access point in its domain, or  other  cards  in
its  add‐hoc  domain.   Use  as the interface rather than Set the
scramble key to The scramble  key  must  be  between  0x0000  and
0xffff.   Both  the  source and the destination must use the same
scramble key in order to communicate.  Display statistics.   When
the optional argument (which must be the last argument to the end
of the command line) is specified as a non‐zero value, statistics
will  be  displayed every seconds.  At the top of each of statis‐
tics, column labels will be displayed.  The first row of  statis‐
tics  will be totals since boot, subsequent lines are deltas from
the previous row.  If is not specified, or is 0 (zero), a  single
page  of statistics will be displayed.  These statistics are more
detailed and include: The domain this card is part of.  Number of
packets received.  Number of overflows detected.  Number of over‐
runs detected.  Number of CRC errors detected.  Random noise  can
cause  these  errors.  Number of framing errors detected.  Number
of generic errors detected.  Number of times a packet was  avail‐
able.  Number of packets requested to be sent.  Number of packets
sent.  Number of packets aborted (not sent within 9 tries).  Num‐
ber of times carrier detect was lost.  Number of generic transmit
errors  detected.   Total  number  of retries.  Number of packets
which were retried times.  Display status read from the hardware.
This option is only available to the super user.  The argument is
used as with the option.  The following fields are displayed A  0
value  implies  no  links.  Probably indicates the quality of the
connection to the access point.  Unknown meaning.  Probably indi‐
cated the quality of the link to the access point.  Unknown mean‐
ing.  Unknown meaning.  The revision numbers of the card.  The ID
of the card.
